## Implementation Priority

| Priority | Category | Rationale |
|----------|----------|-----------|
| 🔴 P0 | **Malformed AI Responses** (§5) | Most likely failure mode in production — Claude output is non-deterministic |
| 🔴 P0 | **JSON Stability** (§1) | Schema is the contract with downstream consumers |
| 🟡 P1 | **Edge Cases** (§4) | Guards against mis-use and missing config |
| 🟡 P1 | **Injection Resistance** (§2) | Security-critical for multi-tenant SaaS |
| 🟢 P2 | **Large Input Handling** (§3) | Important but partly mitigated by Anthropic's own token limits |

---

## Recommended Test Infrastructure

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| **Vitest** or **Jest** | Unit test runner with mocking support |
| **Mock Anthropic client** | Inject fake responses to test §5 without API calls |
| **Zod standalone tests** | Offline schema validation (already exists in [claude.test.ts](file:///d:/ai%20code%20review/src/claude.test.ts)) |
| **Environment stubs** | Override `process.env` to test §4.5–4.6 |

> [!TIP]
> Tests in §1, §4.1–4.4, and §5 can all run **offline** (no API key needed) by mocking the Anthropic client. Only §2 and §3 require live API calls for full confidence.
